From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] pmdomain: qcom: rpmpd: select OPP support

RPMPD supplies performance states and registers its DT OPP tables through
the generic power-domain core. Without PM_OPP, the table-registration
helper is a stub returning -EOPNOTSUPP and the provider fails to probe.

This is visible on a minimal MSM8917/APQ8017 kernel without CPU frequency
scaling: the CX provider reports "Failed to add OPP table for index 0".
Select the OPP framework for this driver's own dependency, without
requiring an unrelated CPU-frequency driver to pull it in.

Base: pem120/linux-msm89x7 a51b91b503307d35902447dd1f90db765372cf3b
Assisted-by: LLM

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/Kconfig b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 	depends on QCOM_SMD_RPM
 	select PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS
 	select PM_GENERIC_DOMAINS_OF
+	select PM_OPP
 	help
 	  QCOM RPM Power domain driver to support power-domains with
 	  performance states. The driver communicates a performance state
